.Sh TERMS
Definitions in the wording of the published piece.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Container, timing, measured output
The three parts that turn something violent or shapeless into output you can
repeat.
For a language model: the harness, the hook, and observability.
.It Harness
Everything a company controls around a model: the instruction file,
permissions, sandbox, hooks and failure record.
.It Hook
A small program that fires at a fixed point in every cycle, such as after
every reply, and checks the output against written rules.
.It Far-end measure
A gauge placed where the value reaches the customer, as opposed to a count
of incidents.
.It Tuning history
The dated record of failures and the fixes they caused; the asset that makes
the same model run well for one team and badly for another.
.It Teach your chat
Changing the workshop around a model (rules, hooks, failure record,
corrected examples) when the weights cannot be changed.
.El
